        <div class="details" id="faq-1">
          <p>Cats purr when they feel content, but they may also purr to comfort themselves or signal that they need help. The sound is part communication and part self-soothing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h3 class="question">
          <button type="button" class="disclosure-trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">
            How much sleep do cats need?
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details" id="faq-2">
          <p>Most cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day. Kittens and older cats often sleep even more because rest helps them grow, recover, and conserve energy.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h3 class="question">
          <button type="button" class="disclosure-trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">
            Why do cats knead blankets?
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="details" id="faq-3">
          <p>Kneading is a comforting habit that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats often knead when they feel relaxed, safe, or especially attached to a person or place.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

